Line 1: I don't understand the character "@".
    say 5 @ 3.
          ^

Line 2: I don't understand "!".
    if x ! y:
         ^
To check that two things are different, write "!=".

Line 3: I don't understand this apostrophe.
    say guests' list.
              ^
An apostrophe can only go inside a word, like isn't or guest's. Text goes in double quotes, like "hello".

Line 4: I don't understand the character "’".
    say it isn’t.
              ^
That's a curly apostrophe. Use a straight one (') instead.

Line 5: I don't understand the character "“".
    say “hi”.
        ^
That's a curly quote. Use straight double quotes (") around text.

